# Railway Debugging Rules (Railway-resident services only)

## Scope

Applies to debugging, log inspection, and runtime troubleshooting of the services that actually
run on Railway. **The web app does not run on Railway.** `ctf-web` (and `ctf-route-weather`) run
on **Render** — see `render.yaml` and rule 123. The services deliberately kept on Railway (cost
decision recorded in `render.yaml`) are:

- **Infisical** — self-hosted secrets manager (single source of truth for secrets)
- **Unleash** — self-hosted feature-flag server
- **Formance ledger** — the ledger service and its Postgres

## Web app ("app not loading") goes to Render, not Railway

When the user says "app not loading", "build error", or similar about the product itself, debug
**Render**, not Railway:

1. Use the Render MCP server, which is what the committed `.mcp.json` configures
   (`"render": { "url": "https://mcp.render.com/mcp" }`, authorized by `RENDER_API_KEY`).
2. Fetch the `ctf-web` service's deploy and runtime logs; check deploy status.
3. `render-debug-agent.yml` (manual dispatch) can also pull Render logs and open a fix PR.
4. Remember the deploy path: `build-images.yml` builds and pushes the GHCR image and triggers the
   Render deploy; `render-deploy.yml` re-pulls the existing image (e.g. to pick up new env vars).

Debug Railway only when the failing piece is Infisical, Unleash, or the Formance ledger (for
example: secrets stopped syncing to Render, flags not resolving, ledger API unreachable at
`FORMANCE_API_URL`).

## Critical: No Railway CLI

The Railway CLI (`railway`) is NOT installed in the Codespaces environment and is not installed by
`.devcontainer/setup.sh`.
**Never attempt `railway logs`, `railway run`, `railway up`, or any `railway` CLI command.**

- Do not try to install the Railway CLI.
- Do not use `npx @railway/cli` or `npm exec @railway/cli`.
- Do not spin in loops checking whether the Railway CLI exists.

## Railway access (when a Railway-resident service is the problem)

The committed `.mcp.json` configures only the Render MCP server — there is no Railway MCP server
entry today. If Railway-side debugging is needed:

- Check with ToolSearch whether any Railway MCP tools are available in the session; if not, the
  Railway dashboard (owner access) is the path — report what needs checking rather than guessing.
- A Railway MCP server (`@railway/mcp-server`, authenticated by a `RAILWAY_API_TOKEN` Codespaces
  secret) can be added to `.mcp.json` if the owner wants agent-side Railway access; do not add it
  without asking.

## Historical note

Earlier versions of this rule described the pre-Render world (web app on Railway,
`ctf/railway.toml` as the deploy entry point, a `the-comic.com` staging environment). All v3 app
services migrated to Render (May 2026); there is no staging deployment (rule 123). Do not use
`ctf/railway.toml` to debug or deploy the web app.
